  "limitations": "The theorem is restricted to the standard uniform one-dimensional nearest-neighbor heat lattice on Z or periodic cycles; the m>=k condition is sufficient, not necessary, and Dirichlet boundaries can fail even after two backward-Euler half-steps. No all-future-step, convergence-order, floating-point, or performance theorem is claimed. Several historically relevant smoothing papers were not inspected end-to-end, leaving residual originality risk.",
